In article <29MAY199314180890@elroy.uh.edu>,\
 st214@elroy.uh.edu (Department of Happy Mammals, Branch Office) writes...
> I've installed 3.1.1 on a vms account.  How do I set the options?  What's
> the name of the configuration file I should put the option settings in, and
> what's the format?

     This is explained in note #2 of the file Install.vms included with
the distribution.  You can define logical name NETHACKOPTIONS with a
quoted string value containing a comma-separated list of options, as in
    $ DEFINE NETHACKOPTIONS "noPickup,Fruit:kumquat,DECgraphics"
or you can put options into a file as most of the micro ports do.  There
are multiple ways to specify that file:
    $ DEFINE NETHACKOPTIONS "@device:[directory]filename"  !note leading '@'
or  $ DEFINE NETHACKINI device:[directory]filename
or  use file SYS$LOGIN:NETHACK.INI
or  use file HOME:NETHACK.CNF  (note that the C run-time library forces
HOME: to match SYS$LOGIN:).  NetHack will use the first one it finds if
you try to specify more than one of these.

     Most options in the file are specified with an `OPTIONS=' prefix like
OPTIONS=nopickup,showexp
but some are prefixed by `GRAPHICS=' and other keywords.  They are described
in the "Guidebook", a documentation file included in the distribution.



